* Savannah had been applying for the show since {{S2|26}}.<ref>https://www.instagram.com/p/DSnN_INAKdS/?hl=en</ref>
* Savannah is the only woman on {{S2|49}} to have never been a member of [[Kele]].
* Savannah is the sixth woman to win four individual [[Immunity Challenge|Immunity Challenges]] in a season, following [[Kelly Wiglesworth]] in {{S2|1}}, [[Jenna Morasca]] in {{S2|6}}, [[Kim Spradlin]] in {{S2|24}}, [[Chrissy Hofbeck]] in {{S2|35}}, and [[Rachel LaMont]] in {{S2|47}}.
** Of the group, Savannah is the only one who won her fourth individual Immunity before the [[Final Immunity Challenge]]. 
** Savannah is the only one who lost the Final Immunity Challenge of the season.
* Savannah is the fourth castaway to win a [[Final Three]] against two opponents of the same gender, following [[Fabio Birza]], Kim Spradlin, and [[Natalie Anderson]].
* Savannah is one of four women to defeat a man in a fire-making challenge, alongside [[Stephenie LaGrossa]] in {{S2|10}}, [[Carolyn Rivera]] in {{S2|30}}, and [[Heidi Lagares-Greenblatt]] in {{S2|44}}.
** Of the group, she is the only one to win her season.
* Savannah is one of seven contestants, alongside [[Russell Hantz]], [[Malcolm Freberg]], [[Michaela Bradshaw]], [[Zeke Smith]], [[Cirie Fields]], and [[Rizo Velovic]], to compete on a future season before their previous season had aired. 
** She is both the first Sole Survivor to achieve this feat and also the first to compete immediately in the following season after their winning season.
** She and Michaela are the only ones to be eliminated before the jury in at least one of those seasons, with Savannah also being the only contestant not to make the jury on their second season.
** Coincidentally, her best placement is higher than the others', while her lowest placement is lower than theirs.
* Savannah is the first person on ''{{dab|Survivor|U.S.}}'' to finish in 22nd place.
* Savannah is the first person to be voted out with a [[Vote Blocker]] in their possession.
* Savannah's elimination in {{S2|50}} happened only 27 days after she won ''Survivor 49'', making this the shortest amount of time a former winner was eliminated following their win.

